Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add per-folder time/name grouping and display-order typeahead

Remember None, Time, or Name grouping per folder, default Downloads to Time,
and migrate existing time-only preferences. Keep folder priority within each
section. Use virtualized grid rows and shared spaced native section headings
in grid, list, and Nautilus chooser views.

Name sections have fixed ascending initial-letter order, with nonletters in #.
Select and cycle prefixes in actual display order while retaining normal search.

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -1,3 +1,36 @@
+Downstream changes (nautilus-typeahead)
+=====================================
+- Add per-folder time and name grouping in both icon and list views, including
+  Nautilus's own Open File/Open Folder chooser. View Options offers No Grouping,
+  Group by Time, and Group by Name (A–Z). Downloads defaults to time grouping.
+- Group by modification time unless a creation/access-time sort is selected.
+  Date sorts control chronological group direction; other sorts order files
+  within newest-first time groups. These are file timestamps, not download dates.
+- Name grouping shows populated initial-letter sections in ascending order.
+  Nonalphabetic initials go under #, accented Latin letters use their base
+  A–Z letter, and non-Latin letters retain their own uppercase headings.
+- Choosing name grouping starts with A–Z filename sorting; the existing Sort
+  options still order items inside each section, never the name-section order.
+- Remember the grouping mode independently for each folder and migrate old
+  time-grouping on/off preferences, including a Downloads opt-out.
+- Refresh section keys and headings after live file changes, including a rename
+  that changes a singleton section's initial without moving any rows.
+- Bind headings directly to their owning view and file data, including pooled
+  unparented headings. Remove extra full-range section notifications from
+  ordinary file-change batches; retain GTK's native section-boundary updates.
+- Keep type-ahead selection in actual display order, including grouped views,
+  and reveal matches outside the visible portion of a large folder.
+- Refresh grouped keyboard navigation after reordering, retain native focus in
+  ungrouped icon views, and register time section titles for translation.
+- Honor folders-before-files within each group instead of collecting all
+  folders in a separate global section.
+- Omit empty sections; headings are not collapsible.
+- Separate sections with standard Adwaita headings and generous vertical
+  spacing, without decorative rules in either view or Nautilus's file chooser.
+- Cycle through matching names when an initial letter is repeated (E-E-E),
+  wrapping in display order. Mixed input remains a prefix search: E-E-X searches
+  for EX. The one-second type-ahead reset and normal search are preserved.
+
